{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791751551,"nonce":"ATUVB/uVOKfSUAaiVqThdnhJdX4=","title":"Expose advanced controller capabilities beyond the standard gamepad layout","message":"Follow-up to the standard API in 84c2359. DualShock and DualSense use positional controls for ordinary game actions, but the current API does not expose touchpad coordinates, gyro/accelerometer samples, adaptive-trigger effects, or structured controller-family/vendor/product metadata for button prompts.\n\nDesign typed capability queries and shared API declarations for supported device-specific features, backed by platform implementations and supporting browser IDL where available. Keep unsupported features explicit; the current dual-motor rumble API does not imply adaptive-trigger support. Do not infer reliable device identity solely from a display name. Include USB/Bluetooth and OS differences in fixture and physical-device verification.\n\nAcceptance: generated bindings remain consistent across runtimes; each added feature can be queried independently; device reconnect invalidates previous handles; supported samples can be copied into reusable buffers; tests and device/platform evidence distinguish implemented support from unavailable capabilities. Coordinate controller-family metadata with ChimpMonk input/prompt work.","files":null}]}